# Every variadic definition in this fixture. va_start reads a register save
# area the translator allocates ('__va_area__' is in the locals) and never
# fills, so selection turns the whole function away before it starts - see
# step 14 of docs/ir-codegen-design.md. Delete these lines once variadic
# definitions land; a name here that stops falling back fails the test.
vaInts
vaDoubles
vaFloats
vaMixed
vaManyBoth
vaNamedFloats
vaFiveNamed
vaSixNamed
vaNamedStruct
vaSmallArgs
vaBigArgs
vaCopied
vaNested
# 'main' is not variadic. It used to fall back for two reasons of its own; step
# 13 took the first away - the struct it passes by value to vaBigArgs and
# vaNamedStruct is now pushed as bytes - and what is left is a float argument
# on the stack, which needs a 'push xmm' that does not exist. Delete this line
# once that lands too.
main
